{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0D7N", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a56dcd85b18633f269a679dd19427e628fb3aa86a62935409a8371075c531780", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we discuss only to what extent a morphism\nof ringed topoi determines an embedding from the derived\ncategory downstairs to the derived category upstairs.\nHere is a typical result.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:dd3c3f235e445ed0309cb6e1ffb3889b351f91bd788a70b92c79f422eda52e42", "unit_id": "tag:0D7N:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0D7N", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : (\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}), \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C}) \\to\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{D}), \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D})$", "MATH_0002": "$D' \\subset D(\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D})$", "MATH_0003": "$K$", "MATH_0004": "$$\nK \\longrightarrow Rf_*Lf^*K\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$D'$", "MATH_0006": "$D(\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D})$", "MATH_0007": "$Lf^* : D' \\to D(\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C})$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-downstairs}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:25eed714e3726bb6bab8fb47d5858ce5f171a9da09cf8b2b0a3a289481c55ae1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e88f9582353456ddd86b4956b79c5712eacff239652653536076024b9b5c85d9", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of ringed topoi.\nConsider the full subcategory <MATH_0002>\nconsisting of objects <MATH_0003> such that\n<MATH_0004>\nis an isomorphism. Then <MATH_0005> is a saturated triangulated strictly full\nsubcategory of <MATH_0006> and the functor\n<MATH_0007> is fully faithful.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:df1634e1849f1b8b16c65dce0c9969acd6807259ba90f6457a32412248004956", "unit_id": "tag:0D7Q:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0D7N", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(Lf^*, Rf_*)$", "MATH_0002": "$D'$", "MATH_0003": "$Lf^*$", "MATH_0004": "$Rf_*$", "MATH_0005": "$Lf^*$", "MATH_0006": "$Rf_*$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{derived-definition-saturated}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{derived-lemma-triangulated-subcategory}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-adjoint}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{categories-lemma-adjoint-fully-faithful}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ed3fdf4aab00cc579ed8150baa77368f0687741cac9b16a795ebcbcb92f12c64", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:85908be5dc3690381d658f909579da98ec285f1700e31188dc77960bb916e42b", "source_text": "See Derived Categories, Definition <REF_0001>\nfor the definition of saturated in this setting. See\nDerived Categories, Lemma <REF_0002>\nfor a discussion of triangulated subcategories.\nThe canonical map of the lemma is the unit of the adjoint\npair of functors <MATH_0001>, see Lemma <REF_0003>.\nHaving said this the proof that <MATH_0002> is a saturated triangulated subcategory\nis omitted; it follows formally from the fact that\n<MATH_0003> and <MATH_0004> are exact functors of triangulated categories.\nThe final part follows formally from\nfact that <MATH_0005> and <MATH_0006> are adjoint; compare with\nCategories, Lemma <REF_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:50e774c1ff1106a880744042ba652edcba2b6eefc2405e49b10c5c5b03fa5492", "unit_id": "tag:0D7Q:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0D7N", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : (\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}), \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C}) \\to\n(\\Sh(\\mathcal{D}), \\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D})$", "MATH_0002": "$D' \\subset D(\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0003": "$K$", "MATH_0004": "$$\nLf^*Rf_*K \\longrightarrow K\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$D'$", "MATH_0006": "$D(\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0007": "$Rf_* : D' \\to D(\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{D})$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-upstairs}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:eb5c7ac234bd78a6da17d62afd5b106530a6e3db04de454d0ba6122e5c9a6476", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a519c5ce24ab58fa3d4437f7fa7452a69ddb02d852ab8928d8a438553858b081", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of ringed topoi.\nConsider the full subcategory <MATH_0002>\nconsisting of objects <MATH_0003> such that\n<MATH_0004>\nis an isomorphism. Then <MATH_0005> is a saturated triangulated strictly full\nsubcategory of <MATH_0006> and the functor\n<MATH_0007> is fully faithful.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:df1634e1849f1b8b16c65dce0c9969acd6807259ba90f6457a32412248004956", "unit_id": "tag:0D7R:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0D7N", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(Lf^*, Rf_*)$", "MATH_0002": "$D'$", "MATH_0003": "$Lf^*$", "MATH_0004": "$Rf_*$", "MATH_0005": "$Lf^*$", "MATH_0006": "$Rf_*$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{derived-definition-saturated}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{derived-lemma-triangulated-subcategory}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-adjoint}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{categories-lemma-adjoint-fully-faithful}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ed3fdf4aab00cc579ed8150baa77368f0687741cac9b16a795ebcbcb92f12c64", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:85908be5dc3690381d658f909579da98ec285f1700e31188dc77960bb916e42b", "source_text": "See Derived Categories, Definition <REF_0001>\nfor the definition of saturated in this setting. See\nDerived Categories, Lemma <REF_0002>\nfor a discussion of triangulated subcategories.\nThe canonical map of the lemma is the counit of the adjoint\npair of functors <MATH_0001>, see Lemma <REF_0003>.\nHaving said this the proof that <MATH_0002> is a saturated triangulated subcategory\nis omitted; it follows formally from the fact that\n<MATH_0003> and <MATH_0004> are exact functors of triangulated categories.\nThe final part follows formally from\nfact that <MATH_0005> and <MATH_0006> are adjoint; compare with\nCategories, Lemma <REF_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:de3d98b1e561ec6ecef36b29c4b5522732f71031fdffc57516a282cf5c061f6e", "unit_id": "tag:0D7R:proof"}
